WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:18.759
Sup my well read ballas? This week we gettin'
our romance on with Don Quixote by Miguel

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.849
de Cervantes.

00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:29.349
Aight, let me get this craziness outta da
way. THIS book is written by Miguel de Cervantes,

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:34.900
who's bout to get straight METAFICTIONAL on
our asses. See, according to the story IN

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.510
the book, the tale of Don Quijote is narrated
by an editor who compiled REAL, different

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:46.350
histories of Don Quijote. Basically, Cervantes
stackin narrative layers like Jay-Z stack

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.780
Benjamins. Da story go like this:

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.910
In an unnamed vilage up in La Mancha, Alonso
Quejano pushin 50, and got a WHOLE lotta

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:59.350
free time on his hands. But instead tryna
throw game at hunnys like most bruthas, Quejano

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.670
spend all his time reading books bout chivalry-
which is da code knights used to live and

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:10.750
die by. Cept, Quejano don't just dabble- he
gets straight obsessed, LITERALLLY readin

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:17.830
all day n' all night. Fool read so much dat
his brain "dries out" and loses his damn mind.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:22.259
Eventually he decide to do jus like da boys
in his books and become a knight errant- ridin

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:26.020
out in to da hood righting all da world's
wrongs.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.099
So homeboy strap up with some janky armor
and hops on his crusty-ass horse ready to

00:01:31.099 --> 00:01:36.660
hit da road. Dude like "Yo horse. Yo name
is now Rocinante. That's way tighter. And

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:43.030
as fo me? I'm gonna be known all throughout
the land as Don Quixote de la Mancha. Helll

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:48.759
yeah." But hold up. First thing every knight
needs is a fine hunny to devote his righteous

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:55.679
deeds to. DQ picks who he think be da choicest
piece in his hood, Aldonza Lorenzo. And since

00:01:55.679 --> 00:02:02.259
he givin out names like candy, he gives her
a new one too: Dulcinea del Toboso. Oh, and

00:02:02.259 --> 00:02:05.500
jus so you know: Don ain't ever actually
said a word to this girl.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:11.379
Then, all the sudden, Don realize he still
missin somethin. What is it? Oh yeah. He ain't

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:17.200
a real knight. Oops. So DQ roll up on an inn,
cuz in his whacked out dome, he thinkin it's

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.880
a castle. He hits up the Lord of the castle
a.k.a the inkeeper, to knight him. The inkeeper

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.670
don't know what da hell is going on, but he
oblige a brutha anyway.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:32.050
So now that he got a woman, a ride, and some
chrome, Don Quijote turnin heads wherever

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:37.190
he go. Cept just a little while later, he
gets his ass handed to him by a buncha salesman

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:42.940
and gotta go back home like a scrub. While
he in bed resting up, his housekeeper, a priest,

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:48.230
and some other homies start BLAZIN' all his
chivalry books hopin he won't do stupid sh**

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.390
like that no mo.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.620
But the Don ain't backin down. He hit up a
local fat-ass peasant named Sancho Panza and

00:02:54.620 --> 00:03:00.400
be like "Say bruh. If you crew up wit me and
be my squire, I'll give you yo own damn kingdom

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.510
cuz you just KNOW I'm gonna be rollin in loot
soon."

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:09.440
So Don Quijote gets up on his horse, Sancho
gets up on his ass, and they get hit da road.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.630
Eventually, they reach a windmill farm, and
Don quijote starts chargin dem suckas yellin'

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.970
his ass off thinkin they giants. Nice man.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:24.230
Don Quixote and Sancho Panzo keep cruisin,
get in all kinda crazy adventures, and receive

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:29.190
some of the nastiest ass whoopins of they
life. Eventually, DQ and Sancho head back

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:35.700
home again. Back at da crib, they start conversatin
with an uppity college grad named Samson Carrasco.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:41.990
Carrasco like "oh sh**. Don Quixote? I read
about you. Man. You famous!" In fact, Carrasco

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:47.630
so geeked dat he decide he gonna try to cure
Don Quijote and save his ass from all dis

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:53.880
Chivalry bullsh**. So in the meantime, Sancho
and the Don can get back to doin their thang,

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.150
cuz Carrasco's bout to spark up a plan.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:01.610
Don Quijote and Sancho gear up for one last
ride, and make a third salley outta town.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.819
This time around, DQ and Sancho get tricked
and trolled at erry turn; especially by some

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:12.450
punkass duke and dutchess. And maybe da worst
trick of all is done by dat boy Carrasco:

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:17.000
to get the Don to come home, dude dressed
himself up and called himself the Knight of

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.970
Mirrors, but just got smacked up by Quijote
in round 1. But now, Carrasco on top of his

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:28.460
game and decide he gonna send Quijote's old
ass packin' once and for all. He straps up

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:33.599
again, calls himself the Knight of the White
Moon, and tricks Don Quijote in to goin back

00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:35.759
home and hangin up his lance.

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:40.710
Feelin like a real piece of sh**, Don Quijote
hits the hay, and after days of sickness,

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.620
he starts callin himself Alonso Quejano again.
He stop giving a damn about chivalry, says

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:52.770
da whole thing was bunk, and eventually dies
a quiet death in bed.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:05:00.969
If you ain't already know, this jam is one
of da most famous novels of all time; and

00:05:00.969 --> 00:05:05.889
it ain't just yo boy Sparky who sayin' that-
scholars ALL up on this book's nuts. Some

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:12.279
say it's da first great novel of world literature-
others say it's the first MODERN work of lit

00:05:12.279 --> 00:05:17.029
eva' written. No matta how you spit it, this
book got some major street cred.

00:05:17.029 --> 00:05:21.610
But is street cred ACTUALLY the same thing
as value or virtue? If we're anything like

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:26.849
da characters who always doggin on books about
chivalry, that answer is a big HAEEEL NO.

00:05:26.849 --> 00:05:33.319
After all, we see what gettin on dat romance
grind 24/7 do to Quijote's mind- turn it to

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:37.889
mush. The priests and Carrascos of the world
would say that he shoulda been reading books

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:43.789
with a moral, not trash dat's just fo sh**s
n giggles. To these dudes Art preachin

00:05:43.789 --> 00:05:46.819
anything else is just harmful and destructive.

00:05:46.819 --> 00:05:52.559
Cervantes wasn't the first intellectual hustla
jivin bout how dangerous art can be. A long

00:05:52.559 --> 00:05:58.259
ass time ago, old school homie Plato was goin
on bout da same thing. According to his character

00:05:58.259 --> 00:06:04.419
Socrates in The Republic, the ideal city knows
it gotta keep dat cray sh** on lockdown

00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:08.930
"if we want the guardians of our city to think
that it's shameful to be easily provoked into

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:14.469
hating one another, we mustn't allow any stories
about gods warring, fighting ,or plotting

00:06:14.469 --> 00:06:19.110
against one another…The young can't distinguish
what is allegorical from what isn't, and the

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.279
opinions they absorb at that age are hard
to erase and apt to become unalterable. For

00:06:24.279 --> 00:06:29.129
these reasons, then, we should probably take
the utmost care to insure that he first stories

00:06:29.129 --> 00:06:33.150
they hear about virtue are the best ones for
them to hear." Republic II.378 c, d, e:

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.400
People, especially the little ones, are just
too monkey see, monkey do. So they should

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:42.639
only watch movies, listen to music, and hit
up plays that gonna teach em a good lesson.

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:48.059
Ugh. You guys have fun in The Republic. Sparky
gonna go set up shop elsewhere. (Sparky picks

00:06:48.059 --> 00:06:50.460
up a copy of The Stranger)

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:55.089
On top of the Don's books not teachin him
a damn thing, another reason his homies always

00:06:55.089 --> 00:06:58.849
hatin on these novels is because they talkin
bout stuff like it's da truth when on the

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:05.129
real it ain't even happen. Which brings me
to one of the top themes of this big ass book,

00:07:05.129 --> 00:07:10.419
deception. Matta fact, a trill critic name
Lionel Trilling (see what I did there?) made

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:16.059
the notorious claim that ALL PROSE FICTION
is a throwback to the main theme of Don Quijote:

00:07:16.059 --> 00:07:18.169
appearance and reality.

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:23.139
First off-Don Quijote CLEARLY got problems
tellin what's real and what ain't. I mean..

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:28.330
dat sh** with the windmills is pretty cray,
amirite? Secondly, brutha gettin trolled all

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:33.110
throughout this book: Sancho always messin
with his head to get outta doin stuff he don't

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:38.430
wanna, the duke and dutchess fool them both,
and Samson Carrasco tricks dat boy TWICE.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:43.580
Don Q even say that deception like dat is
one of the things he rebellin' against:

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:47.719
Blessed the time, and blessed the centuries,
called by the ancients the Golden Age…In

00:07:47.719 --> 00:07:52.879
that time, women…spoke their thoughts of
love from the soul, simply and pretentiously,

00:07:52.879 --> 00:07:58.830
exactly as they thought them, not searching
for elaborate verbal circumlocutions to beautify

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:03.289
them. Truth and simplicity were unmixed with
fraud, deceit, and malice." (59)

00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:10.119
But is deception ALL bad? Is TRUTH the only
way to roll? Naw, baby. All my well-read ballas

00:08:10.119 --> 00:08:16.189
should know by now-ain't nothin wholly good
or wholly bad. Life may have some pretty amazing

00:08:16.189 --> 00:08:21.159
stuff in it, like the Thug Notes book, but
as Don Quijote say: it got some real whack

00:08:21.159 --> 00:08:22.499
stuff in it too.

00:08:22.499 --> 00:08:27.020
Like dis novel repeatedly spittin: one of
da ROUGHEST things people tusssle with is

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:31.710
da fact dat no matta how you play da game
of life, it all gonna end, and even if you

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:36.839
think you got the game sowed up, errything
you know and love can change like DAT (Sparky

00:08:36.839 --> 00:08:41.479
snaps). Sancho actually DOES get a brief shot
at governing his kingdom, but realizes it

00:08:41.479 --> 00:08:47.420
ain't his thang after he chunks deuce, dude
SERIOUSLY falls in a pit the next day:

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:53.230
"Oh! What unexpected things are always happening,
over and over, to those who live in this miserable

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:57.579
world! Who could have predicted that a man
who, yesterday, saw himself the enthroned

00:08:57.579 --> 00:09:02.529
governor of an island, giving orders to servants
and subordinates, would find himself, today,

00:09:02.529 --> 00:09:08.160
buried in a pit, with absolutely no one to
help him, no servant, no subordinate to come

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.199
to his aid? (650)

00:09:09.199 --> 00:09:13.759
And that's why we need Don Quijote. Even if
all dem stories of baller knights fightin

00:09:13.759 --> 00:09:19.339
da good fight are a buncha bullsh**, we still
need em. Cuz only by believing deez lies does

00:09:19.339 --> 00:09:25.949
Don Quijote bring to da world the stuff it's
REALLY lackin I'm talkin dank sh** like integrity,

00:09:25.949 --> 00:09:29.290
loyalty, justice, and persistence in da face
of defeat.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:35.069
That's why it suck so bad to see him step
off the grind at da end of the book. If I

00:09:35.069 --> 00:09:38.630
could say somethin to Cervantes bout this
book's ending, it would probably sound a lot

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:45.449
like what Don Antonio Moreno say to Samson
Carrrasco after Sammy C kicks the Don's ass

00:09:45.449 --> 00:09:46.420
once and for all:

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:50.649
"may God forgive you for the damage you've
done to the whole rest of the world, in trying

00:09:50.649 --> 00:09:55.949
to cure the wittiest lunatic ever seen! Don't
you see, my dear sir, that, whatever utility

00:09:55.949 --> 00:10:00.779
there might be in curing him, it could never
match the pleasure he gives with his madness?"

00:10:00.779 --> 00:10:01.029
(706)

00:10:01.029 --> 00:10:06.790
Now as far as this thug's concerned, it ain't
REALLY Don Quijote that dies at the end, it's

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:13.399
just Alonso Quejano. Don Quijote gonna keep
riding' on, playa- in here and in here. So

00:10:13.399 --> 00:10:18.360
screw da haters-get out there and make da
world a better place, y'all. And I wanna tell

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.019
you bout another channel out there that's
making the world a better place, too—it's

00:10:22.019 --> 00:10:23.190
called THE SCHOOL OF LIFE.

